# --------------------- lnf cnd options ---------------------

block options
name print_input
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
longname print input to listing file
description REPLACE print_input {'{#1}': 'conductance'}

block options
name print_flows
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
longname print calculated flows to listing file
description REPLACE print_flows {'{#1}': 'conductance'}

block options
name save_flows
type keyword
reader urword
optional true
longname save flows for package to budget file
description REPLACE save_flows {'{#1}': 'conductance'}

# --------------------- lnf cnd dimensions ---------------------

block dimensions
name nja
type integer
reader urword
optional false
longname total number of connections
description is the sum of the number of connections and NODES.  When calculating the total number of connections, the connection between node n and node m is considered to be different from the connection between node m and node n.  Thus, NJA is equal to the total number of connections, including n to m and m to n, and the total number of nodes.

# --------------------- lnf cnd griddata ---------------------

block griddata
name conductance
type double precision
shape (nja)
reader readarray
longname conductance for connections
description is the conductance for each connection in the model grid. Conductance values are specified for each entry in the connectivity (JA) array. Values for the diagonal position and for symmetric off-diagonal positions must be specified but are not used.

